# Real sensor/capture data — NEVER commit (CONVENTIONS §3 Privacy, DESIGN_BRIEF §7, LES-003).
# Zeek log trees and anything derived from real traffic: it carries PII, hostnames,
# principals, cert subjects, filenames, and sometimes cleartext credentials.
metadata/
captures/
capture/
zeek-logs/

# NOTE: Zeek metadata archives are NOT listed here. They defend themselves — the
# converter writes a `.gitignore` with `*` into the archive root, the same way
# the feature sink does (LES-011). That covers every artifact including
# `manifest.json` without a blanket rule that would shadow a legitimate manifest
# elsewhere in the tree.

# `aximprint acquire pcap`/`harvest` output — raw pcap, never commit (CONVENTIONS §3
# Privacy). Categorically MORE sensitive than the Zeek metadata above: full packet
# payloads, not derived metadata. Inherited from xtract's own .gitignore as-is
# (docs/WORK_ORDER_merge_xtract_acquire.md step 7) — `--out` defaults to the invoking
# cwd, so these patterns are deliberately UNANCHORED (no leading `/`): they must catch a
# run from the repo root, not just a dedicated output subdirectory. Do not "tidy" them.
*.pcap
*.pcap.part

# Scratch output from a real `aximprint features`/`ingest` run against this repo's own
# root `data/` — repo-root only, deliberately anchored with a leading `/` (fix, this
# merge round): the UNANCHORED `data/` this line used to be matched every `data/`
# anywhere in the tree, silently swallowing `tests/acquire/data/` — a genuine, tracked
# fixture directory (`reference_conn_header.log`) that survived only because it was
# already tracked before the rule existed; every FUTURE fixture placed there would have
# been silently skipped by `git add` with no error. `git check-ignore -v` confirms both
# halves: `data/somefile` still matches (repo-root data/ stays ignored), `tests/acquire/
# data/newfixture.pcap` no longer does.

# Claude workflow sync state
.claude-sync/
.claude/settings.local.json
# ...and the atomic-write temp siblings the harness leaves beside it. The
# exact-filename rule above did not cover these, and one reached a commit.
.claude/settings.local.json.tmp.*

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
*.duckdb
# Covers this project's own evidence-log/feature-sink output AND, coincidentally but
# completely (both patterns are unanchored), xtract's `manifest.jsonl` pcap-extraction
# resume state — confirmed during the merge (docs/WORK_ORDER_merge_xtract_acquire.md
# step 7) rather than assumed; no separate `manifest.jsonl` line is needed.
*.jsonl
/data/
.idea/
.vscode/
